        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Induction is the better electric cooktop for anyone who cooks often: faster, more responsive, more efficient, cooler to live with and easier to clean. Radiant electric is the better buy for tight budgets, occasional cooks and kitchens full of pans that will not pass the magnet test.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Before deciding, test your cookware, check the circuit the new cooktop needs, and be honest about how often you cook. If those three line up, induction is worth the premium. If they do not, a good radiant cooktop will serve you well for years.
          </p>
